= Contributing to LEBOK =

LEBOK is written by its community and reviewed by its editors. Everything
you read here has passed editorial review; everything you propose will get
it.

== How to propose a change ==

# [[Special:CreateAccount|Create an account]] (editing requires login; reading never does).
# Click ''Edit'' on any page — the visual editor opens by default; the <code>&lt;/&gt;</code> icon switches to source/wikitext mode.
# Make your change and save it with a short edit summary saying what and why.
# Your change enters the '''moderation queue'''. It is not visible to readers yet. An editor will approve it, or decline it with a reason — typically within a few days.

To propose a new page (for example, drafting an unstarted knowledge
area), search the exact title you want — e.g.
<code>KA4: &lt;Name&gt;</code> — and follow the red link. New KA pages
should use the section structure of the existing ones:
'''Summary · Scope · Key concepts · Methods and practices · Evidence and
further reading · Related knowledge areas · References'''.

== What makes a change approvable ==

* '''Cite it.''' Claims about what works in learning need sources, via <code>&lt;ref&gt;</code> tags. The [https://capabilitymatters.org/resources LENS resource library] is a good place to find evidence-graded ones.
* '''Reference, not advocacy.''' Write in a neutral, professional register. Contested questions get described as contested, with the positions cited.
* '''Respect draft status.''' Knowledge-area numbering and titles follow the ICICLE working draft; don't rename or renumber KAs — raise that on the page's ''Discussion'' tab instead.

== Discussion ==

Every page has a ''Discussion'' tab. Use it to question content, propose
larger restructurings, or explain a change a moderator declined. Sign talk
posts with <code>~~~~</code>.

== Becoming a trusted editor ==

Contributors with a track record of approvable edits can be granted
'''automoderated''' status (your edits publish immediately) and
'''moderator''' status (you review the queue). Ask on the Discussion tab
of this page, or an editor may simply offer.

== Licensing ==

By saving an edit you agree to release it under this wiki's license (see
the page footer). Don't paste text you don't have the right to license —
summarize and cite it instead.

